# SemText npl-agent — agent definition card, three render variants
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house style shared with the other tag prompts).
# npl-agent is display-only: ONE display mode (a static card whose generated
# header sits above the authored prose) and no view toggles; its variants are
# the render forms the schema and the vocabulary CSS promise. One example page
# per variant, in one frame.
#
# MODE 1 — element form, complete header (the canonical authoring form:
#   name, type, version, extends all authored):
#   visible: one card; a header line above a thin divider carrying, in order:
#     "name ·" small-caps label then the agent identifier in bold;
#     "type ·" label then the archetype in muted text; "NPL@" label then the
#     version in muted text; "extends ·" label then the parent agent name in
#     muted text; below the divider the authored behavioural prose in normal
#     foreground text, fully legible, never rewritten.
#   must never: occlude, blur, or strike any prose; invent interactive chrome
#     (no buttons, toggles, or focus rings — display-only); wrap the four
#     header fields into a second row of labels (the header flexes and may
#     wrap as a whole, but each field stays label-then-value on one line).
# MODE 2 — element form, no parent agent (extends unauthored):
#   visible: the same card with the header line ending after the version —
#     "name ·", "type ·", "NPL@" only. The extends field is simply ABSENT:
#     no gap, no placeholder, no trailing "extends ·" label, no empty slot
#     where the parent name would sit. Body prose identical in position.
#   must never: render an empty extends slot or dimmed placeholder for the
#     missing parent; shift the body prose relative to mode 1 beyond the
#     header's natural shortening.
# MODE 3 — JS-off (vocabulary-only):
#   visible: the authored text as PLAIN PROSE on the page — no card box, no
#     border, no header line, no divider, no generated labels of any kind.
#     (The vocabulary gives the un-upgraded element display:block and nothing
#     else; the JS-off form is the raw authored document text.)
#   must never: show an empty bordered box, a lone divider, upgrade chrome,
#     tier markers, or loading affordances.
#
# Reference snapshots: harness fullpage captures in
# .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-agent/ plus private render-fixture
# captures of the shipped vocabulary CSS (same directory, render-*.jpg;
# see reports/tag-npl-agent.md). The attachments below are live paths.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-agent
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of three reference-page panels in a single row
    illustrating one agent-definition card in its three render variants,
    wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D). Dark
    slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and a
    faint violet radial glow upper-left. Each panel is a dark slate card
    (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, rounded corners, deep soft
    shadow, and a small dim caption bar above it; panels are separated by
    thin slate hairlines.

    The complete-card panels (left and middle) share one anatomy, top to
    bottom: a header line of four small fields — a bold near-white identifier
    preceded by a muted small-caps label ("name"), then a muted archetype
    preceded by the label ("type"), then a muted version preceded by the
    label ("NPL@"), then in the left panel only a muted parent-agent name
    preceded by the label ("extends") — and beneath the header a thin slate
    divider, then two to three lines of bright near-white prose bars (the
    agent's behavioural text) at full opacity. All copy is abstract
    placeholder bars — strictly no letters, digits, or words; the only
    literal glyphs allowed are the label punctuation dots.

    Left panel — MODE 1, the complete card: all four header fields, divider,
    prose bars.
    Middle panel — MODE 2, the parentless card: IDENTICAL in every respect
    except the header line holds exactly three fields (name, type, NPL@) and
    ends there — no fourth field, no gap, no trailing label; the divider and
    prose bars sit at the same relative position.
    Right panel — MODE 3, the JS-off page: the same prose bars as plain body
    text directly on the dark page — NO card box, NO border, NO header line,
    NO divider, NO labels; nothing but unadorned text bars.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words (label punctuation
    dots excepted), watermark, logo, 3D, photorealism, faces, avatars, robot
    mascots, buttons, toggles, switches, progress spinners, focus rings,
    blurred or struck-through text, an empty extends slot or dimmed
    placeholder in the parentless panel, a card box or divider in the JS-off
    panel, occlusion or cover plates anywhere
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, rounded card corners,
    hairline borders, slate and violet palette, three-panel variant
    comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-agent/render-dark-upgraded.jpg
    role: reference
    description: shipped vocabulary render, dark theme — complete card (extends
      authored), parentless card (header ends after NPL@), and the authored
      data-* override card, stacked
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-agent/render-jsoff.jpg
    role: reference
    description: JS-off render — the authored text as plain prose, no card box
      and no header
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-agent/npl-agent-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: the reference page at 1280 — summary and attribute table the
      card examples sit under (stitched capture; treat content, not layout,
      as the reference)

requirements:
  subject: three panels of one agent-definition card — complete four-field
    header, parentless three-field header, and the JS-off plain-prose form
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, near-white
    name and prose, muted slate for type/version/extends labels and values
  composition: three equal panels in one row; identical card anatomy between
    modes 1 and 2 except the missing fourth field; prose bars at the same
    full opacity in all three panels
  do:
    - keep the header as one visual line of label-then-value fields above the
      divider, flexing (wrapping as a whole) rather than stacking labels
    - encode the parentless variant by ABSENCE of the fourth field, never by
      a gap, placeholder, or dimmed slot
    - keep body prose at foreground brightness in every panel; color only the
      small-caps labels and the muted values
    - render the JS-off panel with literally nothing but text bars
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, or logos
    - occlusion, blur, or redaction of any authored line (occlusion belongs to
      spoiler/quiz elements, never to the agent card)
    - interactive chrome — no buttons, toggles, or focus rings (display-only)
    - an empty bordered card or stray divider in the JS-off panel
    - a second row of labels inside one header field

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - no_occlusion
    - parentless_absence
    - jsoff_plain_prose
  criteria:
    no_occlusion:
      weight: 3
      description: Every authored prose line is fully visible in all panels;
        nothing is blurred, struck, or covered
      fail_signals:
        - any blur, strikethrough, cover plate, or redaction bar
        - prose dimmer than the name field in the card panels
    parentless_absence:
      weight: 3
      description: The middle panel's header ends after the version field with
        no gap, trailing label, or placeholder where extends would sit
      fail_signals:
        - an empty slot, dimmed placeholder, or trailing "extends" label in
          the middle panel
        - middle panel structurally different from the left panel beyond the
          missing fourth field
    jsoff_plain_prose:
      weight: 3
      description: The right panel shows plain text bars with no card box,
        divider, header, or labels
      fail_signals:
        - any border, box, divider, or small-caps label in the right panel
        - a lone empty card in the JS-off panel
    header_integrity:
      weight: 2
      description: Header reads as one line of label-then-value fields — bold
        name, muted type, NPL@ version, extends last — above the divider
      fail_signals:
        - labels wrapped into their own row under the values
        - name not visually the boldest header field
        - divider missing or doubled
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 1
      description: Slate Console house palette and hairline borders throughout
      fail_signals:
        - saturated neon accents on body text
        - white cards in the dark panels

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-agent
  - media-prompt
